  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicators:
- Number of areas of intervention identified
-Type of capacity needs identified and type of support required 
- Country specific training resources developed and made available in Arabic 
-Baselines and targets are established for assessing 
- Nb of government officials trained
-Type of sectors benefiting from specialized expertise
-Type of studies/plans carried out
-Nb of experts made available (days per year per sector per activity)
Engagement of key stakeholder in the needs assessment exercise
-Needs assessment of MoLCB, selected local councils and MoI implemented
-Strategic response strategic developed
-Strategic response integrated in national plans for capacity building
-Engagement of women in the assessment process</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2010">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Baseline:
-Weak technical capacity and knowledge of international best practices in specific units/ areas pertaining to government work 
-Weak organizational structures and job descriptions
-Absence of structured inter-ministerial coordination
-Weak capacity of government officials in specific technical and management areas necessary for the government machinery
-Weak capacity to identify immediate technical expertise in a timely manner
-Lack of government data on experts at the international, regional and local level
-Weak institutional connection with the Libyan Diaspora
-Weak institutional capacities at key ministries
-Capacities of institutions in sync with their new mandates after the revolution
-Capacities of institutions unable to respond to urgent planning at the national level</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1 Ministry of Planning with enhanced management capacities

Preparation of 1 Capacity Development Programme and Action Plan 2020-2021 for the Ministry of Planning.

Implementation of the Functional and technical development plan for the MoP staff (Capacity Development Programme and Action Plan 2020-2021) 

100 staff of the MoP improved their technical skills</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">During this year, UNDP has contracted different consultants through CTG and TRANSTEC: human resources officer, technical cooperation officers, an international public state reform consultant, and capacity needs assessment consultant.

UNDP prepared a Capacity Development Programme and Action Plan 2020-2021 for the Ministry of Planning and provided the following eight trainings: Writing report skills, Monitoring and Evaluation; Project Management; Budget preparation; Feasibility study; Electronic archiving; Strategic planning and Financial Auditing. Participants showed an increase understanding and satisfaction in the post evaluation. 

Following an agreement with the MoP based in their needs, different consultants were placed there: three national technical cooperation officers, one national IT, one international public state reform consultant and one international capacity needs assessment consultant. An study with functional review of the pilot ministries and identified support needs to advance Public Reform in Libya was prepared and disseminated and the web-based LCMIS tool was transferred to the new Libyan server.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
